        "claim": "Negative b or d behaves exactly like 0 (range(negative) is empty). b=-1,d=5 produced byte-identical output codes to b=0,d=5; b=5,d=-1 to b=5,d=0.",
        "evidenceCommand": "cd /tmp && source /tmp/probe.sh && for p in \"-1 5\" \"0 5\" \"5 -1\" \"5 0\"; do set -- $p; run 1 $1 2 $2; done",
        "evidenceOutput": "a=1 b=-1 c=2 d=5 | C C C E P C E E C E\na=1 b=0 c=2 d=5 | C C C E P C E E C E\na=1 b=5 c=2 d=-1 | C C C P E C E C E E\na=1 b=5 c=2 d=0 | C C C P E C E C E E",
        "confidence": "certain"
      },
      {
        "claim": "Collapsed line format is exactly: {'values_changed': {'root': {'new_value': <repr(t2)>, 'old_value': <repr(t1)>}}} — 'new_value' precedes 'old_value', 'root' is bare (no bracket path), and the dict reprs are the FULL Python dict reprs with keys in insertion order '0','1',...,'n-1' (so root['9'] is followed by root['10'], NOT lexicographic order). Empty dict renders as {}.",
